  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Loyal Source Government Services obligated $1.9B in FY2026 to date across 20 awards. Loyal Source Government Services recorded an average award size of $95.7M and obligations were up 112.7% year over year. Loyal Source Government Services shows a multi-year increase from $244M in FY21, $173M in FY22, $374M in FY23, $546M in FY24, and $900M in FY25 to $1.9B in FY26. Loyal Source Government Services concentrates most of its FY2026 to date obligations in one agency and one market: the Department of Veterans Affairs at $1.8B and the NAICS category Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $1.8B. Loyal Source Government Services also records smaller but material obligations in the Department of Homeland Security and in Temporary Help Services.",
    "sections": [
