        "heading": "How did Loyal Source Government Services’ obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Loyal Source Government Services obligations were up 112.7% year over year. Loyal Source Government Services fiscal-year obligations progressed from $244M in FY21 to $1.9B in FY26, passing through $173M in FY22, $374M in FY23, $546M in FY24, and $900M in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Loyal Source Government Services’ top buyers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $1.8B. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $75.1M and the Department of Defense obligated $865K; the top NAICS markets are Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $1.8B, Temporary Help Services at $73.6M, and Offices of All Other Miscellaneous Health Practitioners at $1.5M."
      }
